 and Lean D, with prediction markets pricing Talarico near 60%"], "rationale": "The polling average puts Talarico up about 3 points across a dozen recent surveys from pollsters of varied sponsorship, and prediction markets price his win odds near 60 percent. Paxton's fundraising deficit and the flood of outside money attacking him reinforce a modest but real Democratic edge in an open seat.", "watch": "A late shift among Hispanic voters or Republican consolidation behind Paxton could close the gap, while any new Paxton scandal could widen it.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: John Cornyn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Texas's open Senate seat has become one of the most expensive and competitive races of the cycle. State Senator James Talarico leads Attorney General Ken Paxton by roughly three points in recent polling, a striking position for a Democrat in a state that leaned Republican by six points at the baseline. Ratings from national analysts split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets give Talarico about a 60 percent chance of winning.\n\nThe money gap is stark: Talarico has raised nearly $69 million and holds $21.5 million on hand, while Paxton has raised $9 million with under $2 million available. Outside groups have spent $27 million attacking Paxton, reflecting his polarizing record, though his incumbency as attorney general gives him name recognition. Turnout composition and late-breaking voters will decide a race this close.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6697, "margin": 2.08}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6924, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7255, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6997, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6523, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6444, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6983, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7151, "margin": 2.5}]}